Negative control for playback having a PACE (`AC2.5` · `R6-13`).

Runs the scenes back to back with no beat between them — the tight loop the
live drive caught: 0 to 5 in under 60 ms, so no scene is ever seen, the PLAYING
state lasts less than one frame and Pause is unreachable by a human. A player
that finishes before the pointer lifts is not observable playback.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the player spec — `play` holds each scene for the dwell it was given, and
a `pause` issued during that hold leaves the playhead where it stopped.

